Changes to Fish Audio Materials: the runtime/streaming.patch adds an optional
frame callback to the public Drama 3 generator. The integration stages selected
original FP8 routed experts from system RAM without converting checkpoint weights.
ComfyUI nodes, job orchestration, workflows and documentation were added.
Model weights are not distributed in this repository.
The example voices are synthetic model outputs, not recordings of real people.

Changes in ComfyUI-FishAudioDrama3 (fork of https://github.com/Nebuluss/Drama-3 by Nebuluss):
jobs run with ComfyUI's own Python instead of a separate environment (setup_comfyenv.py,
runtime_paths.py; Fish Speech is fetched at the same pinned commit and patched with the same
runtime/streaming.patch); a persistent worker keeps the model loaded between jobs and releases
the GPU when ComfyUI loads another model (worker_manager.py, runtime/worker_protocol.py,
run_drama3_full.py --serve); generation progress and the job log are reported to ComfyUI
(log_echo.py); an FP8 kernel self-check (runtime/selfcheck.py); the routed experts are pinned in
RAM and copied straight to the GPU, with a per-layer GPU cache of recently used experts, and the
audio codec drops three attention masks its modules never read (runtime/fp8_offload.py,
run_drama3_full.py); in fast mode each decode step is replayed from CUDA graphs built on Fish
Speech's own graph code path — the audio decoder, and the backbone in pieces between expert
fetches — the prompt is read in larger chunks, the state a prompt's prefill leaves is reused by
later takes of the same prompt, and the next layer's experts are guessed with its own router and
copied ahead; streamed experts are packed one row per expert (runtime/drama3_generate.py,
runtime/fp8_offload.py, run_drama3_full.py). The Fish Audio Materials
themselves are not modified beyond upstream's runtime/streaming.patch.
